# Lines the language sweep in check-docs.sh may not flag.
#
# Format: <path>%%<substring>
# A hit is suppressed when its path matches an entry and the matched line
# contains that entry's substring.
#
# Every entry carries a comment saying why. An entry without a reason is a
# pattern that was weakened rather than a case that was understood.
#
# Do not widen an entry to cover a class of lines. If a whole file legitimately
# contains German, that file is either a verbatim quote of external output or a
# sign that the language-en module does not fit this project.

# --- The common false positives, present in most English repos --------------

# `die` — the shell error helper, and the English verb.
# `falls` — English "falls back / falls out of sync / falls through".
# `man` — the manual page.
# Add the specific lines here as they come up; there is no blanket entry,
# because a blanket entry stops the check from catching the real cases.

# --- Entries for this repo --------------------------------------------------

# Skill descriptions carry literal trigger phrases in the languages they are
# spoken in. Translating them would stop the skill from being found.
skills/verify/SKILL.md%%description:

# The "Rolle" example is the language rule explaining itself: it names the
# translation layer it exists to prevent.
CLAUDE.md%%("Rolle" in the text

# English "falls back" — the function-word pass cannot tell it from German
# "falls". Listed per line rather than as a pattern exception.
server/internal/ingest/health/provider.go%%falls back
server/internal/ingest/health/shapes_test.go%%falls back
server/internal/storage/source_priority.go%%falls back

# Apple Health delivers workout names localized to the device language.
# workoutNameMap keys are verbatim strings from that API — translating one stops
# it from matching, which is the failure the map exists to prevent.
server/internal/ingest/workouts.go%%"Abkühlen"
server/internal/ingest/workouts.go%%"Flexibilität"
server/internal/ingest/workouts.go%%"Innenräume Radfahren"
server/internal/ingest/workouts.go%%"Innenräume Spaziergang"
server/internal/ingest/workouts.go%%"Outdoor Ausführen"
server/internal/ingest/workouts_test.go%%"Innenräume Radfahren"

# The 2026-09-20 postmortem names the workoutNameMap keys it is about. These are
# verbatim Apple Health workout names, the same strings the map holds; writing
# them in English would describe a key that does not exist.
INCIDENTS.md%%Innenräume Radfahren
